<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI26-RBQA-F002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI26-RBQA-F002" ;
  triage:title "RemoteDeliveryUnconfirmed deepens pre-existing AtmErrorCode crate-layering inversion" ;
  triage:description "ruthless-boundary-qa found during AICH-S6-QA-INTEGRITY-2 (PR #641 @ 584c4c176b7dab82945fb2463f59d06857e58ba2) that crates/atm-storage/src/error_codes.rs:44 -- the RemoteDeliveryUnconfirmed variant added to the storage-owned AtmErrorCode enum as part of AI.26 -- deepens a pre-existing crate-layering inversion (storage crate owning an error code concept that arguably belongs at a higher layer). This predates AI.26; AI.26 correctly followed the established (if architecturally debt-laden) convention rather than introducing a new pattern. This is standing architecture debt, not a regression." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RBQA" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "AICH-S11-QA-CRATELAYER: verified fixed on fix/close-out-round2-hard (f809be26, PR #654). AtmErrorCode/UnknownAtmErrorCode extracted into a new dependency-light atm-error crate; atm-storage and atm-core now depend on and re-export it as pure facades (no duplication, confirmed by workspace-wide grep). No dependency cycle introduced -- independently confirmed via Cargo.toml reads and cargo tree -p atm-core -i atm-error / atm-storage equivalent showing the inverse-dependency tree rooted at atm-error. Import paths preserved via facade re-exports. New architecture guard test (atm_error_code_registry_is_shared_below_storage_and_core) asserts both correct ownership and absence of duplication -- non-vacuous. ruthless-boundary-qa and rust-best-practices-agent both PASS (0 blocking findings). CI fully green (8/8 legs). QA report posted to PR #654." ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T14:35:36Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T15:42:36Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
